mafia 3 might be the most ambitious  title in the series yet set in 1968 in a  fictional New Orleans mafia 3 tells the  story of Lincoln clay a biracial Vietnam  veteran who returns from the war to bind  his home in shambles the black mob the  only thing he has ever called family has  been torn down and the Italian mob has  set up shop with the help of the Irish  mob a self-exiled Italian mobster from  up north and the well-connected leader  of the Haitian gang Lincoln will tear  down the organization from within and  perhaps find a place to be long  recently I got hands-on time for almost  three hours of Mafia 3 and here's what I  saw that I liked this is the first truly  open world Mafia game and it allows you  to tackle each mission in many different  ways similar to how you could and rise  at the Tomb Raider and shadow of Mordor  these missions all take place in the  city of hue or doe which is broken up  into nine districts each district also  has its own crime racket going on  extortion seizing and reselling of  gasoline and construction materials drug  and prostitution rings moonshine brewing  it is all there to get the job done you  can do a number of things from sneaking  into back entrances to running in guns  blazing depending on what path you take  he'll also see different story content  for example when infiltrating the hotel  where a particularly despicable mobster  lives I had two choices I could go to  the garage steal a car and engage in  some subterfuge and sneak up through the  hotel from the basement or I could have  walked into the lobby and just started  shooting each choice offers different  scenarios and in some cases how you  choose to enter a mission can mean life  or death for other characters time and  place matter to see some parts of the  story and by the way I win in guns  blazing  another cool thing you can do is wiretap  areas to reveal the location and type of  enemy's wiretapping essentially unlocks  Lincoln's Intel vision which shows you  where your target is in which enemy is  going to try and call for reinforcements  if they see you through gifting your  three subordinates  that's feet over Cassandra with the  districts and safe houses you conquer  you can unlock new tools for dealing  with these situations veto gives you  better guns and inventory earth will  provide you with Irish mob members for  you to call into fights and Cassandra  will give you the ability to cut the  phone lines in specific areas so enemies  can't call reinforcements there's a ton  of tools at your disposal and they don't  just link to combat as you unlock access  to more vehicles yes those amazing  1960's muscle cars Lincoln can have them  delivered to him wherever he is in the  city these cars handle like boats too  similar to how to handle in real life  and if you can't be bothered to call a  car you can always steal one but you  can't keep it and I can't talk about  mafia 3 without mentioning the  soundtrack developer hangar 13 is packed  the game with licensed tracks from  artists at the time like Creedence  Clearwater Revival Aretha Franklin  Lonnie Youngblood Sam Cooke and more as  I got into my car once the Rolling  Stones paint black came on the radio  it's an amazing experience to ride  around with these songs on the radio or  to walk into a bar and hear them playing  it really grounds the game in real life  I had a lot of fun during my time with  Ma Pa  it feels like it was built on the backs  of games like Tomb Raider and shadow of  Mordor her players unlock skills and  resources at their discretion and have a  delicate balancing act in deciding what  to prioritize and what to forego you can  even choose to kill or spare the enemies  you interrogate building up your empire  or taking no prisoners there's a lot to  do and a lot to keep track of which is  perfect for the open-world setting in  the brief time I had I really felt like  I was making my mark on fictional New  Orleans this time around mafias story is  really up to you
 

